#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:1
msgid "Writing tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:3
msgid ""
"Undici is tuned for a production use case and its default will keep a "
"socket open for a few seconds after an HTTP request is completed to "
"remove the overhead of opening up a new socket. These settings that makes"
" Undici shine in production are not a good fit for using Undici in "
"automated tests, as it will result in longer execution times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:9
msgid ""
"The following are good defaults that will keep the socket open for only "
"10ms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:22
msgid "Guarding against unexpected disconnects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:24
msgid ""
"Undici's `Client` automatically reconnects after a socket error. This "
"means a test can silently disconnect, reconnect, and still pass. "
"Unfortunately,  this could mask bugs like unexpected parser errors or "
"protocol violations. To catch these silent reconnections, add a "
"disconnect guard after creating  a `Client`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:51
msgid ""
"`client.close()` and `client.destroy()` both emit `'disconnect'` events, "
"but those are expected. The guard only fails when a disconnect happens "
"during the active test (i.e., `!client.closed && !client.destroyed` is "
"true)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:55
msgid "Skip the guard for tests where a disconnect is expected behavior, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:57
msgid "Signal aborts (`signal.emit('abort')`, `ac.abort()`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:58
msgid "Server-side destruction (`res.destroy()`, `req.socket.destroy()`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:59
msgid "Client-side body destruction mid-stream (`data.body.destroy()`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:60
msgid "Timeout errors (`HeadersTimeoutError`, `BodyTimeoutError`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:61
msgid "Successful upgrades (the socket is detached from the `Client`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/best-practices_writing-tests.md:62
msgid "Retry/reconnect tests where the disconnect triggers the retry"
msgstr ""

